        "original_id": "f9cb70f6-456b-5cab-8073-6fcc2e22ba93",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Néstor Kirchner, Carlos Menem\n- Places: Argentina, Santa Cruz\n- Roles: President of Argentina, Governor of Santa Cruz\n- Events: Argentine general election, 2003; Presidency of Néstor Kirchner\n\nFacts:\n- Argentina held presidential and parliamentary elections on Sunday, April 27, 2003.\n- Turnout in the 2003 Argentine general election was 78.2%.\n- Néstor Kirchner was the Governor of Santa Cruz during the 2003 Argentine general election.\n- No presidential candidate won outright in the 2003 Argentine general election.\n- Carlos Menem finished first and Néstor Kirchner finished second in the first round of the 2003 Argentine general election.\n- The scheduled runoff in the 2003 Argentine general election was canceled when Carlos Menem withdrew.\n- Carlos Menem's withdrawal handed the presidency to Néstor Kirchner.\n- The Presidency of Néstor Kirchner began on May 25, 2003, when he became President of Argentina.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
